Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:29:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] core+page: Fire Emblem Fates randomizer: background
 make, progress line, owner's rule

Python found once per program run and its real interpreter called directly;
PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX in build/rando-pycache instead of PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE; the
make gets the table cache (build/rando-cache) and --progress. make_run_cancellable
(cancel flag polled every 50 ms; 'progress N' lines stored), run_id_for, discard_run.
Page: a background make of exactly the text Start game would send (proposed random
seed when none is typed): a first guess of the restored last values when the rows are
known, then one 300 ms after the page's values settle; cancelled and deleted on any
change (never a run it did not make); Start game sends the answer the frame the make
of exactly its text is done ('Making your game... N%'), nothing laid before.
Headless: an answer known before the mode pick (rando-answer, FEF_RANDO_ANSWER; test
hook FEF_RANDO_GUESS until FEF_RANDO_GUESS_UNTIL stands for the page's earlier values)
is made in the background, a changed one throws the old guess away, and the pick waits
for the make of exactly its answer, then only lays it; the log gives the ms from the
pick to laid. FEF_HEADLESS_PACE keeps a headless run to the clock for timing tests
(docs/rando/SPEED.md 4 and 5).
